# Filled-in interviews. Each is somebody's plan for their own repository and
# belongs in that repository, next to what it produced -- see answers/README.md,
# which is the one file there that is kept. This is not the reason generated
# checkers are ignored two directories up: those are reproducible from their
# inputs, and nothing a launch produces is reproducible from anything.
answers/*
!answers/README.md

# Assembled prompts written by hand for inspection. `bin/launch prompt` writes
# to stdout and keeps nothing, so anything here was somebody redirecting it.
*.prompt
